[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Objective
[stderr] 
[stderr] Create `projects/<project-slug>/planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md` and
[stderr] `implementation-catalogue-index.json` from the canonical specification.
[stderr] Decompose the first bounded domain chapter (at most 250 implementation
[stderr] contracts) into atomic implementation contracts,
[stderr] using stable IDs such as `IMP-0001`, and create a domain-expansion queue for
[stderr] the remaining chapters. Do not write the final R-series runbooks yet.
[stderr] 
[stderr] An implementation contract is the smallest independently verifiable slice that
[stderr] can be safely handed to an implementation agent. It may be code, content,
[stderr] configuration, research with an explicit output, test automation, migration,
[stderr] documentation, build/release work, or platform certification work.
[stderr] 
[stderr] Derive contracts from the complete domain specification, including product
[stderr] content, tooling, operations, and quality work as first-class implementation
[stderr] work where relevant. An RPG might yield story, character, quest, combat,
[stderr] balancing, localisation, and content-tool contracts; an IDE might yield parser,
[stderr] language-service, debugger, extension-host, workspace, and source-control
[stderr] contracts; an operating system might yield kernel, driver, identity, process,
[stderr] storage, installer, and system-settings contracts. The mechanism must derive,
[stderr] not assume, the appropriate set for any product.
[stderr] 
[stderr] ## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] 
[stderr] - Every record includes title, domain, target(s), requirement IDs, bounded
[stderr]   outcome, prerequisites, files/data/API ownership, forbidden scope,
[stderr]   verification, human/external gate, and estimated authoring complexity.
[stderr] - The index covers foundation, data, domain logic, UI/UX, content, input,
[stderr]   accessibility, security, privacy, performance, observability, tests,
[stderr]   operations, documentation, delivery, and platform-specific work when in
